+/*
+ * Federated authentication, MS-TDS 2.2.6.4 and 2.2.6.5. Only the SECURITYTOKEN
+ * library is implemented: the access token travels inline in LOGIN7, so no
+ * FEDAUTHINFO round trip and no FEDAUTH message type are needed.
+ *
+ * The Options byte holds fFedAuthEcho in bit 0 and bFedAuthLibrary in bits 1-7.
+ * MS-TDS documents the two the other way round; Microsoft confirmed the
+ * documentation is wrong (FreeTDS issue #509) and every shipping client
